title: 'paras: drop the validation-code sentinel from UpcomingParasGenesis'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `UpcomingParasGenesis` stored a full `ParaGenesisArgs`. Onboarding overwrote its
    `validation_code` with an empty vector and then read that emptiness back as a signal that the
    code had already been inserted. It now stores `UpcomingParaGenesis`, holding only the genesis
    head and para kind, and `schedule_para_initialize` drops the `mem::replace`. The code is still
    inserted eagerly via `CurrentCodeHash`. `ParaGenesisArgs` is unchanged and still used by
    chain-spec genesis, the registrar and the sudo wrapper.
crates:
- name: polkadot-runtime-parachains
  bump: minor
- name: rococo-runtime
  bump: patch
- name: westend-runtime
  bump: patch
